theory_blocks.body:
The **circumference** is the boundary of the circle. A **radius** joins the centre to the circumference; all radii are equal. A **diameter** is a chord through the centre ($=2\times$ radius).

A **chord** joins two points on the circumference. A **tangent** is a straight line that touches the circle at exactly one point, the **point of contact**. An **arc** is part of the circumference;

a chord divides the circle into a **minor segment** and a **major segment**, and the angles 'in a segment' are the angles made at the circumference on that side of the chord.

